What:		/sys/power/ddr/abi
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	KAI-Miru kernel maintainers
Description:
		Identifies the active DDR telemetry protocol. H.40 reports
		"aop-ho1.1-transition-ring".

What:		/sys/power/ddr/transitions
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	KAI-Miru kernel maintainers
Description:
		A read-only, chronological snapshot of valid records in the H.40
		AOP H.O.1.1 50-entry DDR transition ring. Event values are 0 for
		frequency-change start, 1 for flush start, and 2 for completion.
		Request and clock-plan byte pairs are printed high-nibble/low-nibble.
		MC and SHUB frequencies come from DDR AOP SMEM item 604 when valid.

What:		/sys/power/ddr/recent_residency
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	KAI-Miru kernel maintainers
Description:
		Residency reconstructed only between completed transitions still
		present in the bounded 50-event AOP ring. This is a diagnostic window,
		not lifetime accounting, and deliberately does not use the standard
		/sys/power/ddr/residency name.

What:		/sys/power/ddr/manager_stats
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	KAI-Miru kernel maintainers
Description:
		Read-only H.O.1.1 DDR-manager counts, recent clock-plan histories,
		and maximum transition/flush timing values.

What:		/sys/power/ddr/clock_plans
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	KAI-Miru kernel maintainers
Description:
		The MC and SHUB clock-plan indices and frequencies decoded from the
		version 1.0 DDR AOP parameter block in SMEM item 604.
